---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import { buildNavigation } from "../lib/docs";

const entries = await getCollection("docs");
const nav = buildNavigation(entries);
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Rye | Agent-Native PostgreSQL Knowledge Graph"
  description="Rye is an open source, agent-native temporal knowledge graph data model for PostgreSQL. It is a schema, not a database, app, or framework."
  nav={nav}
  hideSidebar={true}
>
  <section class="hero-panel home-hero enter">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Agent-native PostgreSQL schema</p>
      <h1>Rye</h1>
      <p class="hero-audience">
        A temporal knowledge graph data model that runs inside your PostgreSQL instance.
      </p>
      <p>
        Rye is open source SQL for tracking entities, relationships, activities, evolving
        assertions, and source evidence across connected systems. The CLI now installs
        Rye, syncs portable plugin and skill metadata, and gives agents a context bundle
        before they write.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/docs/getting-started/quickstart/">Start Fast</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/docs/reference/cli/">CLI Reference</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://github.com/BLTGV/project-rye">GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="schema-map" aria-label="Rye core schema map">
      <div class="schema-map-header">
        <span>Portable context</span>
        <strong>Schema plus catalogs</strong>
      </div>
      <div class="schema-map-grid">
        <span class="schema-node schema-node--strong">nodes</span>
        <span class="schema-node">edges</span>
        <span class="schema-node">events</span>
        <span class="schema-node">event_participants</span>
        <span class="schema-node">assertions</span>
        <span class="schema-node">artifacts</span>
      </div>
      <div class="schema-map-footer">
        <code>rye_agent_context()</code>
        <code>rye_plugin_catalog()</code>
        <code>rye_skill_catalog()</code>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stats-grid stats-grid--four enter enter-d1" aria-label="Core Rye capabilities">
    <article>
      <h2>Fast Start CLI</h2>
      <p>Bootstrap local Docker or a remote PostgreSQL database, then write `.rye.env`.</p>
      <code class="stat-code">./scripts/rye init local</code>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Portable Catalogs</h2>
      <p>Plugins, skills, and capabilities sync into Rye metadata for discovery.</p>
      <code class="stat-code">catalog capabilities</code>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Agent Context</h2>
      <p>A single command returns core catalog, scopes, source inventory, and policy.</p>
      <code class="stat-code">./scripts/rye context</code>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Scope-First Agents</h2>
      <p>Create an active onboarding scope before source intake or fact promotion.</p>
      <code class="stat-code">onboard create</code>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="capability-section enter enter-d2" aria-labelledby="implementation-heading">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Current implementation</p>
      <h2 id="implementation-heading">What the repo now ships</h2>
      <p>
        The site now tracks the portable CLI path from the latest commit: hosted
        bootstrap, `./scripts/rye`, plugin and skill manifests, capability catalogs,
        agent context, source inventory, and conformance smoke tests.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="capability-grid">
      <article class="capability-card">
        <h3>CLI v1</h3>
        <p>
          `init local`, `init remote`, `doctor`, `status`, `context`, `catalog`, and
          `sources` commands make first-run setup and agent discovery scriptable.
        </p>
        <a href="/docs/reference/cli/">CLI reference</a>
      </article>
      <article class="capability-card">
        <h3>Portable Catalogs</h3>
        <p>
          `rye_plugin_catalog()`, `rye_skill_catalog()`, and `rye_capability_catalog()`
          expose installable behavior as queryable Rye metadata.
        </p>
        <a href="/docs/reference/data-dictionary/">Data dictionary</a>
      </article>
      <article class="capability-card">
        <h3>Agent Context Bundle</h3>
        <p>
          `rye_agent_context()` combines catalog, scope selection, source inventory,
          pending confirmations, and compiled policy for agents.
        </p>
        <a href="/docs/reference/onboarding/">Onboarding scopes</a>
      </article>
      <article class="capability-card">
        <h3>Metadata Smoke Tests</h3>
        <p>
          New conformance suites validate portable catalog functions and the CLI JSON
          paths used by agents and scripts.
        </p>
        <a href="/docs/model/core-contract-and-conformance/">Conformance kit</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-grid enter enter-d3">
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Operational Flow</h2>
      <p>From bootstrap to agent-readable context.</p>
      <ol class="steps-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Install Rye</strong>
          <span>Use the hosted bootstrap or the repo-local CLI.</span>
          <code>curl -fsSL https://projectrye.dev/onboard | sh</code>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Check the instance</strong>
          <span>Verify the database, synced metadata, and available capabilities.</span>
          <code>./scripts/rye doctor</code> + <code>catalog skills</code>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Create the first scope</strong>
          <span>Record purpose, boundaries, default review policy, and enabled plugins.</span>
          <code>./scripts/rye onboard create</code>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Hand context to agents</strong>
          <span>Return catalogs, scopes, source inventory, confirmations, and policy.</span>
          <code>./scripts/rye context --json</code>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Start Here</h2>
      <ul class="start-here-links">
        <li>
          <a href="/docs/getting-started/quickstart/">Quickstart</a>
          <span>Use the new CLI flow for install, metadata, scope, and context.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/docs/reference/cli/">CLI Reference</a>
          <span>Commands for init, catalogs, context, sources, status, and doctor.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/docs/reference/data-dictionary/">Data Dictionary</a>
          <span>Tables, views, functions, and the portable catalog helpers.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/docs/model/security/">Security Model</a>
          <span>RLS, field redaction, classification gates, and Supabase behavior.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/docs/reference/roadmap/">Roadmap</a>
          <span>Onboarding, plugins, evidence, retention, admin, and graph quality.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="truth-strip enter enter-d4" aria-label="What Rye is not">
    <div>
      <span>Not a database</span>
      <p>Rye runs in standard PostgreSQL.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <span>Not an application</span>
      <p>Domain tools remain the operational UI.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <span>Not a framework</span>
      <p>The deliverable is SQL.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-section enter enter-d5">
    <div class="cta-card">
      <h2>Own the knowledge graph your agents use.</h2>
      <p>
        Start with the CLI quickstart, then use portable catalogs and conformance tests
        to keep your Rye instance predictable as plugins, skills, and scopes grow.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/docs/getting-started/quickstart/">Start Fast</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/docs/model/core-contract-and-conformance/">Conformance Kit</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
